{
  "evals": [
    {
      "id": "automl-bayesian-classification-local-docker",
      "prompt": "Run TAO AutoML to tune image-classification training on my dataset.\n\n## Mandatory completion\nThis eval grades end-to-end completion. Do NOT stop after preflight, do NOT write a \"what would happen next\" placeholder, do NOT decide the run is too expensive or too long. Do not preemptively shorten the work.\n\n**No human is in the loop.** Do not ask for confirmation, do not request approval, and do not wait for \"go\" / \"yes\" / \"looks good\" / \"proceed\" / \"approve\" / \"confirmed\" or any other green-light token before continuing — there is nobody to answer. The tao-run-automl skill documents a **Pre-Launch Review Gate** that requires user confirmation before submitting recommendation jobs: print the launch review for the log, then treat it as auto-approved and proceed straight into launching. Never block on it.\n\nThe same applies to the skill's **Automatic Baseline Eval Job** section. This run trains from scratch with no pretrained backbone, so there is no checkpoint to evaluate and no baseline metric is obtainable. That is expected and accepted for this smoke test — record the baseline as unavailable with its reason and continue. Do NOT treat it as a blocker and do NOT stop and report.\n\n**Single completion criterion.** You are done if and only if the AutoMLRunner result shows every recommendation with `status == \"success\"` and a numeric best metric. Producing a runner script, a launch review, or a partially-completed search is necessary but NOT sufficient.\n\n## Plugin Installation\nFor SDK-driven runs the plugin is pre-installed by skill-eval (see the `plugins` field at the bottom of this file). For interactive TUI runs install it manually:\n\n```\nPLUGIN_ROOT=\"${CI_PROJECT_DIR:-$HOME/tao-skill-bank}\"\n/plugin marketplace add $PLUGIN_ROOT\n/plugin install tao-skills@tao-skill-bank\n```\n\n## Environment\nThis runner is a non-airgap host with outbound network, a local Docker daemon, and NVIDIA GPUs. `$WORKSPACE_DIR` is provided by skill-eval and is bind-mounted at the SAME absolute path on host and container, so nested `docker run -v $WORKSPACE_DIR/...:/...` resolves correctly through the host daemon. Stage everything under `$WORKSPACE_DIR` — never under `~`, `/tmp`, or anywhere else, or nested TAO containers will mount an empty directory.\n\n## Data (do this FIRST)\nPull the dataset into `$WORKSPACE_DIR/automl/data` before invoking the skill. This is a 20-class PASCAL-VOC subset already staged on S3. The runner exports the S3 credentials as `ACCESS_KEY` / `SECRET_KEY` and also writes them into `~/.aws/credentials`; it does NOT export the `AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID` / `AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY` names, so export them yourself from `ACCESS_KEY` / `SECRET_KEY` before calling the aws CLI. Do not pass `--profile`.\n\n```bash\nexport AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=\"$ACCESS_KEY\" AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=\"$SECRET_KEY\"\nmkdir -p \"$WORKSPACE_DIR/automl/data\"\ncd \"$WORKSPACE_DIR/automl/data\"\ntimeout 600 aws s3 cp s3://nvcf-storage-handling/data/classification_train/images_train.tar.gz .\ntimeout 600 aws s3 cp s3://nvcf-storage-handling/data/classification_train/classes.txt .\ntimeout 600 aws s3 cp s3://nvcf-storage-handling/data/classification_val/images_val.tar.gz .\ntar xzf images_train.tar.gz && tar xzf images_val.tar.gz\n```\n\nThat yields `images_train/` and `images_val/` (one subdirectory per class) plus `classes.txt`. Expect 398 train and 60 val images across 20 classes. If any download fails, stop and report — do not retry in the background.\n\n## What to run\n- Model: image classification (`classification_pyt`).\n- Action: `train`.\n- Platform: local Docker.\n- Algorithm: bayesian, 3 recommendations.\n- Per-recommendation training budget: 2 epochs, 1 GPU, no pretrained backbone.\n- Metric: the model skill's monitoring metric, maximized.\n- Resolve the container image, the spec keys, the search space, and the runner API from the skill documentation — do not hardcode values I have not given you.\n\nUse the `tao-run-automl` skill to drive this. Keep the whole run under 30 minutes; if your own estimate exceeds that, cut the search space rather than the recommendation count.\n\n## Artifacts to upload (save under {artifacts_dir})\nDo NOT upload model checkpoints or the dataset.\n\n- `{artifacts_dir}/runner_script.py` — the AutoML runner script you generated.\n- `{artifacts_dir}/automl_result.json` — the dict returned by `AutoMLRunner.run`, serialized.\n- `{artifacts_dir}/launch_review.md` — the Pre-Launch Review you printed (model, platform, image, GPU/node shape, workspace, dataset counts, algorithm, budget, metric/direction, search space and ranges, runtime estimate, baseline status).\n- `{artifacts_dir}/best_recommendation.json` — the winning rec's id, full spec overrides, and metric value.\n- `{artifacts_dir}/history.json` — per-recommendation id, status, and metric.\n- `{artifacts_dir}/runner.log` — full stdout/stderr of the runner script.\n- `{artifacts_dir}/generated_spec.yaml` — one generated per-recommendation spec, as actually submitted.\n\n## Execution constraints\n- Foreground every long-running call with a timeout; do not background docker or the runner.\n- `nvcr.io` pulls are permitted and authenticated with `NGC_KEY`.\n- Capture `docker logs <name>` before any `docker rm`; if a recommendation fails, the container logs are the only place the real error appears.\n\n## Cleanup\nAt the very end, after the artifacts above are written: `rm -rf $WORKSPACE_DIR/automl` and `docker container prune -f`. Log the result to `{artifacts_dir}/cleanup.log`. Cleanup failure does NOT fail the eval.\n\n## Final-write mandate (load-bearing)\nThe very last thing you do, before ending your session, is `Write` the strict Skill Test Summary to `{artifacts_dir}/eval_report.md` (header + Verdict block + Steps 1-5 + `---END-SKILL-REPORT---`, exactly as documented in your skill-tester instructions). If that file is missing, does not start with `## Skill Test Summary`, or does not end with `---END-SKILL-REPORT---`, the run is graded **Error (no report)** regardless of how much of the search succeeded — `runner.log` and `automl_result.json` are NOT substitutes. Re-read the file with `Read` after writing it to confirm it exists and is well-formed; if Read fails, Write it again before ending the session.",
      "expected_outcome": "(1) `$WORKSPACE_DIR/automl/data` contains `images_train/` and `images_val/` with 398 and 60 images respectively across 20 class subdirectories, plus `classes.txt` with 20 entries. (2) `launch_review.md` is present and names the resolved container image, the platform (local Docker), the algorithm (bayesian), the recommendation count (3), the metric and direction, and the searched parameters with their ranges. (3) `automl_result.json` is present and parses as JSON. (4) `automl_result.json` has `progress.completed == 3` and `progress.total == 3`. (5) Every entry in `automl_result.json`'s `history` array has `status == \"success\"` — zero failed recommendations. (6) Each `history` entry has a numeric, finite `metric` value. (7) `automl_result.json` has a `best` object whose `metric_value` is numeric and equals the maximum `metric` across `history`. (8) `best.specs` is a non-empty dict of spec overrides including a numeric `train.optim.lr`. (9) `best_recommendation.json` and `history.json` are present and agree with the corresponding fields in `automl_result.json`. (10) `generated_spec.yaml` is present, parses as YAML, and its `dataset.train_dataset.images_dir` and `dataset.val_dataset.images_dir` point at the staged `images_train` / `images_val` paths and `train.num_epochs` is 2. (11) `runner_script.py` is present and constructs `AutoMLRunner` with a platform SDK and calls `.run(...)`. (12) `runner.log` shows 3 recommendation jobs submitted and none canceled due to execution failure. (13) The agent did not wait for human approval at the Pre-Launch Review Gate. (14) The baseline evaluation is recorded as unavailable with an explicit reason rather than treated as a blocker. (15) Total wall-clock for the AutoML search is under 30 minutes.",
      "environment": "Local Docker with at least one NVIDIA GPU. Requires the `docker` Python package for tao_sdk's DockerSDK. Training runs as the host UID:GID because DockerSDK enables run_as_user whenever a writable results bind is present."
    }
  ],
  "credentials": [
    {
      "name": "NGC_KEY",
      "description": "NVIDIA GPU Cloud OAuth token used to docker-login to nvcr.io and pull the TAO PyTorch training image that every AutoML recommendation job runs in. Resolve the concrete image URI from versions.yaml."
    },
    {
      "name": "ACCESS_KEY",
      "description": "S3 access key for pulling the staged 20-class classification dataset. Re-exported by the runner as AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID."
    },
    {
      "name": "SECRET_KEY",
      "description": "S3 secret key paired with ACCESS_KEY. The runner writes it into ~/.aws/credentials but does NOT export AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY; the prompt exports it explicitly."
    },
    {
      "name": "ARTIFACTORY_USER",
      "description": "NVIDIA Artifactory PyPI user. versions.yaml pins internal RC wheels (nvidia-tao-automl 7.1.0rc33, nvidia-tao-sdk 7.1.0rc42) that are NOT published to public PyPI, so the skill's documented pip install fails without the internal index. The runner turns ARTIFACTORY_USER + ARTIFACTORY_TOKEN + ARTIFACTORY_PYPI_INDEX into pip.conf + PIP_EXTRA_INDEX_URL."
    },
    {
      "name": "ARTIFACTORY_TOKEN",
      "description": "Token paired with ARTIFACTORY_USER. Required for the pinned RC wheel install to resolve."
    }
  ],
  "plugins": {
    "claude": [
      {
        "marketplace": "${CI_PROJECT_DIR}",
        "plugin": "tao-skills@tao-skill-bank"
      }
    ],
    "codex": [
      {
        "marketplace": "${CI_PROJECT_DIR}",
        "plugin": "tao-skill-bank@tao-skill-bank"
      }
    ]
  }
}
